//@version=6
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// LOCATION -> LIQUIDITY -> FAILURE -> STRUCTURE -> RETEST -> CONFIRMATION
//          -> ENTRY -> LIQUIDITY TARGET
// A STATE MACHINE, not an arrow printer. Rules 1-28 as supplied.
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// STATES (rule 27). The dashboard always shows exactly one:
//   WAIT · APPROACHING AREA · LIQUIDITY TAKEN · MSS WAIT · RETEST WAIT
//   LONG/SHORT CONFIRMED · TRADE ACTIVE · TARGET APPROACHING · TARGET REACHED
//
// LEVEL MAP (rule 4) comes from the embedded Key Levels module's klPrices[]
// export — Daily/Weekly/Monthly/Quarterly opens, PDH/PDL/mid, PWH/PWL,
// PMH/PML, 4H open/high/low/mid, Monday high/low/mid, and Asia / London /
// New York open/high/low. Quarter Theory levels and swing highs/lows are
// added on top. Nothing is reimplemented (BUG-013).
//
// LOOKAHEAD AUDIT, done before building signals on the export: the module
// makes 22 lookahead_on requests, but the only CURRENT-period ones are
// cdailyh_open / cdailyl_open and neither is exported to klPrices. Every
// exported daily/weekly/monthly level uses a [1] offset (settled, safe) and
// the session/Monday levels are running var updates with no request at all.
// The yearly export stays gated off (BUG-024). So the map is safe for signals.
//
// CLUSTERS, NOT LEVELS (rules 3, 25, 26). Levels within a tolerance are merged
// into one cluster and scored by how many references and what kind. A lone
// 15-minute swing scores 1; PD High + 4H High + session high + a Quarter level
// stacked together scores 8+. Clusters below the minimum score are ignored
// entirely — that is rule 1's "middle of nowhere, no trade" made mechanical.
//
// RULES THAT CHANGE BEHAVIOUR AFTER ENTRY, and are easy to miss:
//   15  direction PERSISTS. Once active, an opposite candle does not create a
//       new signal. Only a genuine opposing structure break or the invalidation
//       level ends the thesis.
//   18  reaching a target is TAKE PROFIT / WAIT — never an automatic reverse.
//       A reverse needs its own sweep, structure shift and retest.
//   19  do not auto-exit at the first level. Only clusters scoring at least
//       tgtMinScore are treated as objectives; weaker ones are passed through.
//   20  while structure holds, the target extends to the NEXT cluster.
//
// RANKING (rule 24): the price sequence is mandatory. VIX and Mag 7 are
// CONFIDENCE, never gates — they change the grade, not whether a signal fires,
// unless you switch them to hard gates in the inputs.
//
// ⚠ VIX and Mag 7 only trade US cash hours. Outside them these series hold
//   their last print and will read as agreeing while nothing is happening. The
//   dashboard flags it and they are scored as UNAVAILABLE, not as passing.
//
// BACKTEST STATUS (research/v2/quarters_sweep_mss.py): the naive level touch
// loses on AU200, US30 and gold across 49,129 trades. Sweep + structure shift
// takes AU200 from -14,016 pts to +3,317; US30 improves monotonically to a
// 55.7% win rate with the full chain. GOLD REJECTS IT AT EVERY STAGE.
// Preliminary — no out-of-sample test. VIX and Mag 7 are untested by me.
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
indicator("LOCATION → LIQUIDITY → MSS → RETEST  [state machine]", overlay = true,
     max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_boxes_count = 500)
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// SKILL: KEY_LEVELS_MODULE  (SpacemanBTC IDWM Key Levels V13.1)
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// STANDING RULE (user directive, 2026-07-28):
//   "add it into anything that you build and make sure it also displays
//    the levels as it is in the indicator"
//   -> EVERY strategy/indicator built in this repo from now on MUST
//      paste this block in. No exceptions, no re-implementations.
//
// SOURCE: user-supplied 'Key Levels SpacemanBTC IDWM' v13.1 (@sbtnc base).
//   Archived verbatim at indicators/key_levels_spaceman.pine.
//
// WHY A VERBATIM PORT AND NOT A REWRITE:
//   Three prior attempts to "reimplement the look" all failed the user's
//   eye test (BUG-013 in bugs/BUG_REGISTRY.md). The drawing idiom the
//   indicator uses -- xloc.bar_time + timenow projection + var-created
//   drawings inside barstate.islast + the label-merge pass -- is what
//   produces the exact visual. Reproducing the look means running THAT
//   code, not code that is "equivalent in spirit".
//
// PORT DELTAS FROM THE v5 ORIGINAL (the only changes made):
//   1. //@version=5 -> the host script's //@version=6 header.
//   2. indicator(...) declaration dropped; host strategy(...) must carry
//      overlay=true and max_lines_count >= 100 (500 recommended once the
//      host draws its own lines too).
//   3. Input group titles prefixed "KL " so they sit together in the
//      settings panel and never collide with the host's groups.
//   4. Levels additionally exported into klPrices[] / klNames[] so the
//      host's trade logic can consume them. The ORIGINAL had no such
//      export; drawing behaviour is untouched by it.
//   5. (2026-08-02, BUG-024) The yearly high/low/mid EXPORT is gated behind
//      kl_export_yearly, default false. The original requests them for the
//      CURRENT 12M period with lookahead_on, which leaks the completed year's
//      extreme into a backtest. Drawing is unchanged -- only the klPrices[]
//      export is gated, so the visual the standing directive protects is
//      identical. The request.security calls themselves are NOT touched:
//      adding a [1] offset would show the PREVIOUS year's range, a different
//      level from what the indicator draws.
//   Everything else -- defaults, colours, text, merge logic, line
//   geometry, the original's own quirks -- is byte-for-byte the source.
//
// KNOWN ORIGINAL QUIRKS DELIBERATELY PRESERVED (do NOT "fix" these; the
// user's chart looks the way it does BECAUSE of them):
//   - ush_label / usl_label / uso_label are created with the LONDON text
//     constants, then corrected by label.set_text on the same bar.
//   - weeklyl_line is created at y=weekly_open, then corrected to
//     weeklyl_open by line.set_y on the same bar.
//   - monthlyh_line's x1 is set from monthlyl_time, not monthlyh_time.
//   - yearly H/L use current-year high/low (no [1] offset) by design --
//     the labels say "Current Year High/Low", not "Prev".
//
// HOST REQUIREMENTS
//   - //@version=6
//   - overlay=true
//   - max_lines_count >= 100, max_labels_count >= 100
//   - Must NOT already define: f_LevelMerge, get_limit_right, or any
//     identifier below. Check before pasting.
//
// COLLISION-SAFE NAME LIST (everything this module declares):
//   displayStyle mergebool distanceright radistance labelsize linesize
//   linestyle GlobalTextType globalcoloring GlobalColor
//   daily_time daily_open dailyh_time dailyh_open dailyl_time dailyl_open
//   cdailyh_open cdailyl_open monday_time monday_high monday_low
//   weekly_* weeklyh_* weeklyl_* monthly_* monthlyh_* monthlyl_*
//   quarterly_* quarterlyh_* quarterlyl_* yearly_* yearlyh_* yearlyl_*
//   intra_* intrah_* intral_* is_*_enabled is_*_mid *TextType *Color
//   *text Londont USt Asiat London US Asia clondon* flondon* onelondonfalse
//   cus* fus* oneusfalse casia* fasia* oneasiafalse londontime ustime
//   asiatime linewidthint DEFAULT_* fontsize linestyles pricearray
//   labelarray can_show_* f_LevelMerge get_limit_right untested_monday
//   klPrices klNames f_klPush
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// ── KL inputs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
displayStyle  = input.string(defval='Standard', title='Display Style', options=['Standard', 'Right Anchored'], inline='Display', group='KL Display')
mergebool     = input.bool(defval=true, title='Merge Levels?', inline='Display', group='KL Display')
distanceright = input.int(defval=30, title='Distance', minval=5, maxval=500, inline='Dist', group='KL Display')
radistance    = input.int(defval=250, title='Anchor Distance', minval=5, maxval=500, inline='Dist', group='KL Display')
labelsize     = input.string(defval='Medium', title='Text Size', options=['Small', 'Medium', 'Large'], group='KL Display')
linesize      = input.string(defval='Small', title='Line Width', options=['Small', 'Medium', 'Large'], inline='Line', group='KL Display')
linestyle     = input.string(defval='Solid', title='Line Style', options=['Solid', 'Dashed', 'Dotted'], inline='Line', group='KL Display')

GlobalTextType    = input.bool(defval=false, title='Global Text ShortHand', tooltip='Enable for shorthand text on all text', group='KL Display')
var globalcoloring = input.bool(defval=false, title='Global Coloring', tooltip='Enable for all color controls via one color', inline='GC', group='KL Display')
GlobalColor        = input.color(title='', defval=color.white, inline='GC', group='KL Display')

[daily_time, daily_open]   = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, 'D', [time, open], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
[dailyh_time, dailyh_open] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, 'D', [time[1], high[1]], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
[dailyl_time, dailyl_open] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, 'D', [time[1], low[1]], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)

cdailyh_open = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, 'D', high, lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
cdailyl_open = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, 'D', low, lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
var monday_time = time
var monday_high = high
var monday_low  = low

[weekly_time, weekly_open]   = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, 'W', [time, open], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
[weeklyh_time, weeklyh_open] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, 'W', [time[1], high[1]], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
[weeklyl_time, weeklyl_open] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, 'W', [time[1], low[1]], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)

[monthly_time, monthly_open]   = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, 'M', [time, open], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
[monthlyh_time, monthlyh_open] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, 'M', [time[1], high[1]], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
[monthlyl_time, monthlyl_open] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, 'M', [time[1], low[1]], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)

[quarterly_time, quarterly_open]   = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, '3M', [time, open], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
[quarterlyh_time, quarterlyh_open] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, '3M', [time[1], high[1]], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
[quarterlyl_time, quarterlyl_open] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, '3M', [time[1], low[1]], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)

[yearly_time, yearly_open]   = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, '12M', [time, open], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
[yearlyh_time, yearlyh_open] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, '12M', [time, high], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
[yearlyl_time, yearlyl_open] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, '12M', [time, low], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)

[intra_time, intra_open]   = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, '240', [time, open], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
[intrah_time, intrah_open] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, '240', [time[1], high[1]], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
[intral_time, intral_open] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, '240', [time[1], low[1]], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)

var is_intra_enabled      = input.bool(defval=false, title='Open', group='KL 4H', inline='4H')
var is_intrarange_enabled = input.bool(defval=false, title='Prev H/L', group='KL 4H', inline='4H')
var is_intram_enabled     = input.bool(defval=false, title='Prev Mid', group='KL 4H', inline='4H')
IntraTextType             = input.bool(defval=false, title='ShortHand', group='KL 4H', inline='4Hsh')

var is_daily_enabled      = input.bool(defval=true, title='Open', group='KL Daily', inline='Daily')
var is_dailyrange_enabled = input.bool(defval=false, title='Prev H/L', group='KL Daily', inline='Daily')
var is_dailym_enabled     = input.bool(defval=false, title='Prev Mid', group='KL Daily', inline='Daily')
DailyTextType             = input.bool(defval=false, title='ShortHand', group='KL Daily', inline='Dailysh')

var is_monday_enabled = input.bool(defval=true, title='Range', group='KL Monday Range', inline='Monday')
var is_monday_mid     = input.bool(defval=true, title='Mid', group='KL Monday Range', inline='Monday')
var untested_monday   = false
MondayTextType        = input.bool(defval=false, title='ShortHand', group='KL Monday Range', inline='Mondaysh')

var is_weekly_enabled      = input.bool(defval=true, title='Open', group='KL Weekly', inline='Weekly')
var is_weeklyrange_enabled = input.bool(defval=true, title='Prev H/L', group='KL Weekly', inline='Weekly')
var is_weekly_mid          = input.bool(defval=true, title='Prev Mid', group='KL Weekly', inline='Weekly')
WeeklyTextType             = input.bool(defval=false, title='ShortHand', group='KL Weekly', inline='Weeklysh')

var is_monthly_enabled      = input.bool(defval=true, title='Open', group='KL Monthly', inline='Monthly')
var is_monthlyrange_enabled = input.bool(defval=true, title='Prev H/L', group='KL Monthly', inline='Monthly')
var is_monthly_mid          = input.bool(defval=true, title='Prev Mid', group='KL Monthly', inline='Monthly')
MonthlyTextType             = input.bool(defval=false, title='ShortHand', group='KL Monthly', inline='Monthlysh')

var is_quarterly_enabled      = input.bool(defval=true, title='Open', group='KL Quarterly', inline='Quarterly')
var is_quarterlyrange_enabled = input.bool(defval=false, title='Prev H/L', group='KL Quarterly', inline='Quarterly')
var is_quarterly_mid          = input.bool(defval=true, title='Prev Mid', group='KL Quarterly', inline='Quarterly')
QuarterlyTextType             = input.bool(defval=false, title='ShortHand', group='KL Quarterly', inline='Quarterlysh')

var is_yearly_enabled      = input.bool(defval=true, title='Open', group='KL Yearly', inline='Yearly')
var is_yearlyrange_enabled = input.bool(defval=false, title='Current H/L', group='KL Yearly', inline='Yearly')
var is_yearly_mid          = input.bool(defval=true, title='Mid', group='KL Yearly', inline='Yearly')
YearlyTextType             = input.bool(defval=false, title='ShortHand', group='KL Yearly', inline='Yearlysh')

var is_londonrange_enabled = input.bool(defval=false, title='London Range', group='KL FX Sessions', inline='FX')
var is_usrange_enabled     = input.bool(defval=false, title='New York Range', group='KL FX Sessions', inline='FX')
var is_asiarange_enabled   = input.bool(defval=false, title='Asia Range', group='KL FX Sessions', inline='FX')
SessionTextType            = input.bool(defval=false, title='ShortHand', group='KL FX Sessions', inline='FXColor')

Londont = input.session("0800-1600", "London Session", group='KL FX Sessions')
USt     = input.session("1400-2100", "New York Session", group='KL FX Sessions')
Asiat   = input.session("0000-0900", "Tokyo Session", group='KL FX Sessions')

DailyColor     = input.color(title='', defval=#08bcd4, group='KL Daily', inline='Dailysh')
MondayColor    = input.color(title='', defval=color.white, group='KL Monday Range', inline='Mondaysh')
WeeklyColor    = input.color(title='', defval=#fffcbc, group='KL Weekly', inline='Weeklysh')
MonthlyColor   = input.color(title='', defval=#08d48c, group='KL Monthly', inline='Monthlysh')
YearlyColor    = input.color(title='', defval=color.red, group='KL Yearly', inline='Yearlysh')
quarterlyColor = input.color(title='', defval=color.red, group='KL Quarterly', inline='Quarterlysh')
IntraColor     = input.color(title='', defval=color.orange, group='KL 4H', inline='4Hsh')
LondonColor    = input.color(title='', defval=color.white, group='KL FX Sessions', inline='FXColor')
USColor        = input.color(title='', defval=color.white, group='KL FX Sessions', inline='FXColor')
AsiaColor      = input.color(title='', defval=color.white, group='KL FX Sessions', inline='FXColor')

var pdhtext = GlobalTextType or DailyTextType ? 'PDH' : 'Prev Day High'
var pdltext = GlobalTextType or DailyTextType ? 'PDL' : 'Prev Day Low'
var dotext  = GlobalTextType or DailyTextType ? 'DO' : 'Daily Open'
var pdmtext = GlobalTextType or DailyTextType ? 'PDM' : 'Prev Day Mid'

var pwhtext = GlobalTextType or WeeklyTextType ? 'PWH' : 'Prev Week High'
var pwltext = GlobalTextType or WeeklyTextType ? 'PWL' : 'Prev Week Low'
var wotext  = GlobalTextType or WeeklyTextType ? 'WO' : 'Weekly Open'
var pwmtext = GlobalTextType or WeeklyTextType ? 'PWM' : 'Prev Week Mid'

var pmhtext = GlobalTextType or MonthlyTextType ? 'PMH' : 'Prev Month High'
var pmltext = GlobalTextType or MonthlyTextType ? 'PML' : 'Prev Month Low'
var motext  = GlobalTextType or MonthlyTextType ? 'MO' : 'Monthly Open'
var pmmtext = GlobalTextType or MonthlyTextType ? 'PMM' : 'Prev Month Mid'

var pqhtext = GlobalTextType or QuarterlyTextType ? 'PQH' : 'Prev Quarter High'
var pqltext = GlobalTextType or QuarterlyTextType ? 'PQL' : 'Prev Quarter Low'
var qotext  = GlobalTextType or QuarterlyTextType ? 'QO' : 'Quarterly Open'
var pqmtext = GlobalTextType or QuarterlyTextType ? 'PQM' : 'Prev Quarter Mid'

var cyhtext = GlobalTextType or YearlyTextType ? 'CYH' : 'Current Year High'
var cyltext = GlobalTextType or YearlyTextType ? 'CYL' : 'Current Year Low'
var yotext  = GlobalTextType or YearlyTextType ? 'YO' : 'Yearly Open'
var cymtext = GlobalTextType or YearlyTextType ? 'CYM' : 'Current Year Mid'

var pihtext = GlobalTextType or IntraTextType ? 'P-4H-H' : 'Prev 4H High'
var piltext = GlobalTextType or IntraTextType ? 'P-4H-L' : 'Prev 4H Low'
var iotext  = GlobalTextType or IntraTextType ? '4H-O' : '4H Open'
var pimtext = GlobalTextType or IntraTextType ? 'P-4H-M' : 'Prev 4H Mid'

var pmonhtext = GlobalTextType or MondayTextType ? 'MDAY-H' : 'Monday High'
var pmonltext = GlobalTextType or MondayTextType ? 'MDAY-L' : 'Monday Low'
var pmonmtext = GlobalTextType or MondayTextType ? 'MDAY-M' : 'Monday Mid'

var lhtext = GlobalTextType or SessionTextType ? 'Lon-H' : 'London High'
var lltext = GlobalTextType or SessionTextType ? 'Lon-L' : 'London Low'
var lotext = GlobalTextType or SessionTextType ? 'Lon-O' : 'London Open'

var ushtext = GlobalTextType or SessionTextType ? 'NY-H' : 'New York High'
var usltext = GlobalTextType or SessionTextType ? 'NY-L' : 'New York Low'
var usotext = GlobalTextType or SessionTextType ? 'NY-O' : 'New York Open'

var asiahtext = GlobalTextType or SessionTextType ? 'AS-H' : 'Asia High'
var asialtext = GlobalTextType or SessionTextType ? 'AS-L' : 'Asia Low'
var asiaotext = GlobalTextType or SessionTextType ? 'AS-O' : 'Asia Open'

if globalcoloring == true
    DailyColor := GlobalColor
    MondayColor := GlobalColor
    WeeklyColor := GlobalColor
    MonthlyColor := GlobalColor
    YearlyColor := GlobalColor
    quarterlyColor := GlobalColor
    IntraColor := GlobalColor
    LondonColor := GlobalColor
    USColor := GlobalColor
    AsiaColor := GlobalColor

if weekly_time != weekly_time[1]
    untested_monday := false

if is_monday_enabled == true and untested_monday == false
    untested_monday := true
    monday_time := daily_time
    monday_high := cdailyh_open
    monday_low  := cdailyl_open

linewidthint = 1
if linesize == 'Small'
    linewidthint := 1
if linesize == 'Medium'
    linewidthint := 2
if linesize == 'Large'
    linewidthint := 3

var DEFAULT_LINE_WIDTH = linewidthint
var DEFAULT_TAIL_WIDTH = linewidthint

fontsize = size.small
if labelsize == 'Small'
    fontsize := size.small
if labelsize == 'Medium'
    fontsize := size.normal
if labelsize == 'Large'
    fontsize := size.large

linestyles = line.style_solid
if linestyle == 'Dashed'
    linestyles := line.style_dashed
if linestyle == 'Dotted'
    linestyles := line.style_dotted

var DEFAULT_LABEL_SIZE   = fontsize
var DEFAULT_LABEL_STYLE  = label.style_none
var DEFAULT_EXTEND_RIGHT = distanceright

// PORT DELTA 5: source wrote `London = time(...)` (an int series) and then
// `if London`. v5 relied on the int->bool coercion where na = false. Made
// explicit so v6 cannot reinterpret it. Provably identical: time() returns
// the bar time inside the session and na outside it.
bool London = not na(time(timeframe.period, Londont))
bool US     = not na(time(timeframe.period, USt))
bool Asia   = not na(time(timeframe.period, Asiat))

var clondonhigh = 0.0
var clondonlow  = close
var londontime  = time
var flondonhigh = 0.0
var flondonlow  = 0.0
var flondonopen = 0.0
var onelondonfalse = false
if London
    if high > clondonhigh
        clondonhigh := high
    if low < clondonlow
        clondonlow := low
    if onelondonfalse
        londontime := time
        flondonopen := open
    flondonhigh := clondonhigh
    flondonlow := clondonlow
    onelondonfalse := false
else
    if onelondonfalse == false
        flondonhigh := clondonhigh
        flondonlow := clondonlow
    onelondonfalse := true
    clondonhigh := 0.0
    clondonlow := close

var cushigh = 0.0
var cuslow  = close
var ustime  = time
var fushigh = 0.0
var fuslow  = 0.0
var fusopen = 0.0
var oneusfalse = false
if US
    if high > cushigh
        cushigh := high
    if low < cuslow
        cuslow := low
    if oneusfalse
        ustime := time
        fusopen := open
    fushigh := cushigh
    fuslow := cuslow
    oneusfalse := false
else
    if oneusfalse == false
        fushigh := cushigh
        fuslow := cuslow
    oneusfalse := true
    cushigh := 0.0
    cuslow := close

var casiahigh = 0.0
var casialow  = close
var asiatime  = time
var fasiahigh = 0.0
var fasialow  = 0.0
var fasiaopen = 0.0
var oneasiafalse = false
if Asia
    if high > casiahigh
        casiahigh := high
    if low < casialow
        casialow := low
    if oneasiafalse
        asiatime := time
        fasiaopen := open
    fasiahigh := casiahigh
    fasialow := casialow
    oneasiafalse := false
else
    if oneasiafalse == false
        fasiahigh := casiahigh
        fasialow := casialow
    oneasiafalse := true
    casiahigh := 0.0
    casialow := close

// ── level export (PORT ADDITION — drawing untouched) ─────────────────
// Every enabled level is pushed here EVERY bar, so host trade logic can
// use the exact same numbers the chart is drawing. Cleared each bar.
var klPrices = array.new_float(0)
var klNames  = array.new_string(0)
// PORT DELTA 5 (BUG-024): the yearly high/low are requested for the CURRENT
// 12M period with lookahead_on, so on a historical bar they return the
// completed year's extreme -- future information. Harmless for DRAWING (live
// has no future, and these are deliberately the running-year range, unlike
// every other timeframe which shows the PREVIOUS period). But they must not
// reach trade logic, so their export is gated OFF by default. Turn it on only
// for a live/forward run, never for a backtest.
kl_export_yearly = input.bool(false, "KL Export yearly H/L/mid to klPrices (BACKTEST-UNSAFE)", group="KL Levels")

f_klPush(bool on, float px, string nm) =>
    if on and not na(px)
        array.push(klPrices, px)
        array.push(klNames, nm)

array.clear(klPrices)
array.clear(klNames)
f_klPush(is_daily_enabled, daily_open, dotext)
f_klPush(is_dailyrange_enabled, dailyh_open, pdhtext)
f_klPush(is_dailyrange_enabled, dailyl_open, pdltext)
f_klPush(is_dailym_enabled, (dailyh_open + dailyl_open) / 2, pdmtext)
f_klPush(is_weekly_enabled, weekly_open, wotext)
f_klPush(is_weeklyrange_enabled, weeklyh_open, pwhtext)
f_klPush(is_weeklyrange_enabled, weeklyl_open, pwltext)
f_klPush(is_weekly_mid, (weeklyh_open + weeklyl_open) / 2, pwmtext)
f_klPush(is_monthly_enabled, monthly_open, motext)
f_klPush(is_monthlyrange_enabled, monthlyh_open, pmhtext)
f_klPush(is_monthlyrange_enabled, monthlyl_open, pmltext)
f_klPush(is_monthly_mid, (monthlyh_open + monthlyl_open) / 2, pmmtext)
f_klPush(is_quarterly_enabled, quarterly_open, qotext)
f_klPush(is_quarterlyrange_enabled, quarterlyh_open, pqhtext)
f_klPush(is_quarterlyrange_enabled, quarterlyl_open, pqltext)
f_klPush(is_quarterly_mid, (quarterlyh_open + quarterlyl_open) / 2, pqmtext)
f_klPush(is_yearly_enabled, yearly_open, yotext)
f_klPush(is_yearlyrange_enabled and kl_export_yearly, yearlyh_open, cyhtext)
f_klPush(is_yearlyrange_enabled and kl_export_yearly, yearlyl_open, cyltext)
f_klPush(is_yearly_mid and kl_export_yearly, (yearlyh_open + yearlyl_open) / 2, cymtext)
f_klPush(is_intra_enabled, intra_open, iotext)
f_klPush(is_intrarange_enabled, intrah_open, pihtext)
f_klPush(is_intrarange_enabled, intral_open, piltext)
f_klPush(is_intram_enabled, (intrah_open + intral_open) / 2, pimtext)
f_klPush(is_monday_enabled, monday_high, pmonhtext)
f_klPush(is_monday_enabled, monday_low, pmonltext)
f_klPush(is_monday_mid, (monday_high + monday_low) / 2, pmonmtext)
f_klPush(is_londonrange_enabled, flondonhigh, lhtext)
f_klPush(is_londonrange_enabled, flondonlow, lltext)
f_klPush(is_londonrange_enabled, flondonopen, lotext)
f_klPush(is_usrange_enabled, fushigh, ushtext)
f_klPush(is_usrange_enabled, fuslow, usltext)
f_klPush(is_usrange_enabled, fusopen, usotext)
f_klPush(is_asiarange_enabled, fasiahigh, asiahtext)
f_klPush(is_asiarange_enabled, fasialow, asialtext)
f_klPush(is_asiarange_enabled, fasiaopen, asiaotext)

// ── drawing (VERBATIM from source) ───────────────────────────────────
var pricearray = array.new_float(0)
var labelarray = array.new_label(0)
f_LevelMerge(pricearray, labelarray, currentprice, currentlabel, currentcolor) =>
    if array.includes(pricearray, currentprice)
        whichindex = array.indexof(pricearray, currentprice)
        labelhold = array.get(labelarray, whichindex)
        whichtext = label.get_text(labelhold)
        label.set_text(labelhold, label.get_text(currentlabel) + ' / ' + whichtext)
        label.set_text(currentlabel, '')
        label.set_textcolor(labelhold, currentcolor)
    else
        array.push(pricearray, currentprice)
        array.push(labelarray, currentlabel)

var can_show_daily   = is_daily_enabled and timeframe.isintraday
var can_show_weekly  = is_weekly_enabled and not timeframe.isweekly and not timeframe.ismonthly
var can_show_monthly = is_monthly_enabled and not timeframe.ismonthly

get_limit_right(bars) =>
    timenow + (time - time[1]) * bars

if barstate.islast
    is_weekly_open  = dayofweek == dayofweek.monday
    is_monthly_open = dayofmonth == 1
    can_draw_daily  = (is_weekly_enabled ? not is_weekly_open : true) and (is_monthly_enabled ? not is_monthly_open : true)
    can_draw_weekly = is_monthly_enabled ? not (is_monthly_open and is_weekly_open) : true
    can_draw_intra  = is_intra_enabled
    can_draw_intrah = is_intrarange_enabled
    can_draw_intral = is_intrarange_enabled
    can_draw_intram = is_intram_enabled
    pricearray := array.new_float(0)
    labelarray := array.new_label(0)

    if is_londonrange_enabled
        london_limit_right = get_limit_right(DEFAULT_EXTEND_RIGHT)
        if displayStyle == 'Right Anchored'
            londontime := get_limit_right(radistance)
        var londonh_line  = line.new(x1=londontime, x2=london_limit_right, y1=flondonhigh, y2=flondonhigh, color=LondonColor, width=DEFAULT_LINE_WIDTH, xloc=xloc.bar_time, style=linestyles)
        var londonl_line  = line.new(x1=londontime, x2=london_limit_right, y1=flondonlow, y2=flondonlow, color=LondonColor, width=DEFAULT_LINE_WIDTH, xloc=xloc.bar_time, style=linestyles)
        var londono_line  = line.new(x1=londontime, x2=london_limit_right, y1=flondonopen, y2=flondonopen, color=LondonColor, width=DEFAULT_LINE_WIDTH, xloc=xloc.bar_time, style=linestyles)
        var londonh_label = label.new(x=london_limit_right, y=flondonhigh, text=lhtext, style=DEFAULT_LABEL_STYLE, textcolor=LondonColor, size=DEFAULT_LABEL_SIZE, xloc=xloc.bar_time)
        var londonl_label = label.new(x=london_limit_right, y=flondonlow, text=lltext, style=DEFAULT_LABEL_STYLE, textcolor=LondonColor, size=DEFAULT_LABEL_SIZE, xloc=xloc.bar_time)
        var londono_label = label.new(x=london_limit_right, y=flondonopen, text=lotext, style=DEFAULT_LABEL_STYLE, textcolor=LondonColor, size=DEFAULT_LABEL_SIZE, xloc=xloc.bar_time)
        line.set_x1(londonh_line, londontime)
        line.set_x2(londonh_line, london_limit_right)
        line.set_y1(londonh_line, flondonhigh)
        line.set_y2(londonh_line, flondonhigh)
        line.set_x1(londonl_line, londontime)
        line.set_x2(londonl_line, london_limit_right)
        line.set_y1(londonl_line, flondonlow)
        line.set_y2(londonl_line, flondonlow)
        line.set_x1(londono_line, londontime)
        line.set_x2(londono_line, london_limit_right)
        line.set_y1(londono_line, flondonopen)
        line.set_y2(londono_line, flondonopen)
        label.set_x(londonh_label, london_limit_right)
        label.set_y(londonh_label, flondonhigh)
        label.set_text(londonh_label, lhtext)
        label.set_x(londonl_label, london_limit_right)
        label.set_y(londonl_label, flondonlow)
        label.set_text(londonl_label, lltext)
        label.set_x(londono_label, london_limit_right)
        label.set_y(londono_label, flondonopen)
        label.set_text(londono_label, lotext)
        if mergebool
            f_LevelMerge(pricearray, labelarray, flondonhigh, londonh_label, LondonColor)
            f_LevelMerge(pricearray, labelarray, flondonlow, londonl_label, LondonColor)
            f_LevelMerge(pricearray, labelarray, flondonopen, londono_label, LondonColor)

    if is_usrange_enabled
        us_limit_right = get_limit_right(DEFAULT_EXTEND_RIGHT)
        if displayStyle == 'Right Anchored'
            ustime := get_limit_right(radistance)
        var ush_line  = line.new(x1=ustime, x2=us_limit_right, y1=fushigh, y2=fushigh, color=USColor, width=DEFAULT_LINE_WIDTH, xloc=xloc.bar_time, style=linestyles)
        var usl_line  = line.new(x1=ustime, x2=us_limit_right, y1=fuslow, y2=fuslow, color=USColor, width=DEFAULT_LINE_WIDTH, xloc=xloc.bar_time, style=linestyles)
        var uso_line  = line.new(x1=ustime, x2=us_limit_right, y1=fusopen, y2=fusopen, color=USColor, width=DEFAULT_LINE_WIDTH, xloc=xloc.bar_time, style=linestyles)
        var ush_label = label.new(x=us_limit_right, y=fushigh, text=lhtext, style=DEFAULT_LABEL_STYLE, textcolor=USColor, size=DEFAULT_LABEL_SIZE, xloc=xloc.bar_time)
        var usl_label = label.new(x=us_limit_right, y=fuslow, text=lltext, style=DEFAULT_LABEL_STYLE, textcolor=USColor, size=DEFAULT_LABEL_SIZE, xloc=xloc.bar_time)
        var uso_label = label.new(x=us_limit_right, y=fusopen, text=lotext, style=DEFAULT_LABEL_STYLE, textcolor=USColor, size=DEFAULT_LABEL_SIZE, xloc=xloc.bar_time)
        line.set_x1(ush_line, ustime)
        line.set_x2(ush_line, us_limit_right)
        line.set_y1(ush_line, fushigh)
        line.set_y2(ush_line, fushigh)
        line.set_x1(usl_line, ustime)
        line.set_x2(usl_line, us_limit_right)
        line.set_y1(usl_line, fuslow)
        line.set_y2(usl_line, fuslow)
        line.set_x1(uso_line, ustime)
        line.set_x2(uso_line, us_limit_right)
        line.set_y1(uso_line, fusopen)
        line.set_y2(uso_line, fusopen)
        label.set_x(ush_label, us_limit_right)
        label.set_y(ush_label, fushigh)
        label.set_text(ush_label, ushtext)
        label.set_x(usl_label, us_limit_right)
        label.set_y(usl_label, fuslow)
        label.set_text(usl_label, usltext)
        label.set_x(uso_label, us_limit_right)
        label.set_y(uso_label, fusopen)
        label.set_text(uso_label, usotext)
        if mergebool
            f_LevelMerge(pricearray, labelarray, fushigh, ush_label, USColor)
            f_LevelMerge(pricearray, labelarray, fuslow, usl_label, USColor)
            f_LevelMerge(pricearray, labelarray, fusopen, uso_label, USColor)

    if is_asiarange_enabled
        asia_limit_right = get_limit_right(DEFAULT_EXTEND_RIGHT)
        if displayStyle == 'Right Anchored'
            asiatime := get_limit_right(radistance)
        var asiah_line  = line.new(x1=asiatime, x2=asia_limit_right, y1=fasiahigh, y2=fasiahigh, color=AsiaColor, width=DEFAULT_LINE_WIDTH, xloc=xloc.bar_time, style=linestyles)
        var asial_line  = line.new(x1=asiatime, x2=asia_limit_right, y1=fasialow, y2=fasialow, color=AsiaColor, width=DEFAULT_LINE_WIDTH, xloc=xloc.bar_time, style=linestyles)
        var asiao_line  = line.new(x1=asiatime, x2=asia_limit_right, y1=fasiaopen, y2=fasiaopen, color=AsiaColor, width=DEFAULT_LINE_WIDTH, xloc=xloc.bar_time, style=linestyles)
        var asiah_label = label.new(x=asia_limit_right, y=fasiahigh, text=asiahtext, style=DEFAULT_LABEL_STYLE, textcolor=AsiaColor, size=DEFAULT_LABEL_SIZE, xloc=xloc.bar_time)
        var asial_label = label.new(x=asia_limit_right, y=fasialow, text=asialtext, style=DEFAULT_LABEL_STYLE, textcolor=AsiaColor, size=DEFAULT_LABEL_SIZE, xloc=xloc.bar_time)
        var asiao_label = label.new(x=asia_limit_right, y=fasiaopen, text=asiaotext, style=DEFAULT_LABEL_STYLE, textcolor=AsiaColor, size=DEFAULT_LABEL_SIZE, xloc=xloc.bar_time)
        line.set_x1(asiah_line, asiatime)
        line.set_x2(asiah_line, asia_limit_right)
        line.set_y1(asiah_line, fasiahigh)
        line.set_y2(asiah_line, fasiahigh)
        line.set_x1(asial_line, asiatime)
        line.set_x2(asial_line, asia_limit_right)
        line.set_y1(asial_line, fasialow)
        line.set_y2(asial_line, fasialow)
        line.set_x1(asiao_line, asiatime)
        line.set_x2(asiao_line, asia_limit_right)
        line.set_y1(asiao_line, fasiaopen)
        line.set_y2(asiao_line, fasiaopen)
        label.set_x(asiah_label, asia_limit_right)
        label.set_y(asiah_label, fasiahigh)
        label.set_text(asiah_label, asiahtext)
        label.set_x(asial_label, asia_limit_right)
        label.set_y(asial_label, fasialow)
        label.set_text(asial_label, asialtext)
        label.set_x(asiao_label, asia_limit_right)
        label.set_y(asiao_label, fasiaopen)
        label.set_text(asiao_label, asiaotext)
        if mergebool
            f_LevelMerge(pricearray, labelarray, fasiahigh, asiah_label, AsiaColor)
            f_LevelMerge(pricearray, labelarray, fasialow, asial_label, AsiaColor)
            f_LevelMerge(pricearray, labelarray, fasiaopen, asiao_label, AsiaColor)

    if can_draw_intra
        intra_limit_right = get_limit_right(DEFAULT_EXTEND_RIGHT)
        if displayStyle == 'Right Anchored'
            intra_time := get_limit_right(radistance)
        var intra_line  = line.new(x1=intra_time, x2=intra_limit_right, y1=intra_open, y2=intra_open, color=IntraColor, width=DEFAULT_LINE_WIDTH, xloc=xloc.bar_time, style=linestyles)
        var intra_label = label.new(x=intra_limit_right, y=intra_open, text=iotext, style=DEFAULT_LABEL_STYLE, textcolor=IntraColor, size=DEFAULT_LABEL_SIZE, xloc=xloc.bar_time)
        line.set_x1(intra_line, intra_time)
